  "body": "## What\n\nBooks the fourteenth VERIFIED edge: `pq-named-refusals -> fm-refusal-ledger`, receipt `SuperInstance/fleet-murmur#8`.\n\n**Currency event.** fleet-murmur PR #8 (*\"Refusal-events ledger: draft-kamimura-scitt-refusal-events-03 × pong-quilt named refusals\"*, MERGED 2026-09-30T19:31:12Z, merge `b21a4a46`) lands `docs/ietf-kamimura-refusal-events-ledger.md` in the to-node's repo, citing **SuperInstance/pong-quilt by name** at an anchored, pinned site: PQ_PIN repo constant + corpus table pinned to pong-quilt main merge `52b42b4` (six named refusal kinds present-tense grepped at the pin), with `tests/test_refusal_events_ledger.py` running a FAIL-first corpus pin so a drifted citation trips RED instead of passing silently. Draft source re-verified current 2026-10-01 (still `-03`).\n\nWeight law met in the citing repo's merge (edge #2 precedent — the merge is in fleet-murmur, so the edge books **into** fleet-murmur). Never self-upgraded: Casey's merge earned the edge; this PR books it. The 17:49 pulse's org note recorded *\"mints pq->fm refusal-ledger edge\"* at merge time.\n\n## Changes\n- **seed.mjs**: +2 nodes (`pq-named-refusals`, `fm-refusal-ledger`), +1 VERIFIED edge — claim carries CURRENCY EARNED 2026-09-30 + merge sha `b21a4a4` + kill switch; provenance `null` (the corpus lives on pong-quilt main, the receipt is the fleet-murmur merge)\n- **pins.mjs**: 17→18 edges, 13→14 VERIFIED, fleet-murmur first **triple-inbound** repo (honesty#2 + qgs-adapter#3 + refusal-ledger#8), pong-quilt third outgoing edge, +**Pin 3o** (5 currency checks), panel prose updated\n- **REFERRAL_GRAPH.md**: fourteenth-edge log entry\n\n## Evidence\n- FAIL-first: new pins against pristine main tip → **11 RED** (edge not found, counts 17≠18, view mass fm 2≠3)\n- `node experiments/referral_graph.pins.mjs` → **113/113 green** (108 on main + 5 new)\n- `node experiments/referral_graph.pins.mjs --live` → **114/114 green** — 25 receipts audited live, all MERGED (incl. fleet-murmur#8)\n\n## Ordering note\nThe ds-esign-drift booking (edge #14) rides open PR #32. Counts here assume main without it; if #32 lands first, this branch rebases (md ordinals follow merge order — the chain hash, not prose, is canonical). Casey-gated either way.\n",
